## 1. Core Principles

### The Economics of Claude — Understand This First

Claude charges **separately for input and output tokens**, and the ratio is asymmetric:

| Token Type | Sonnet 4.6 | Opus 4.6 | Haiku 4.5 |
|---|---|---|---|
| Input | $3.00 / 1M | $15.00 / 1M | $0.80 / 1M |
| Output | $15.00 / 1M | $75.00 / 1M | $4.00 / 1M |
| Cached Input | $0.30 / 1M | $1.50 / 1M | $0.08 / 1M |
| Batch Input | $1.50 / 1M | $7.50 / 1M | $0.40 / 1M |

> ⚡ **Output tokens cost 5× more than input tokens.** Every unnecessary word Claude writes costs more than 5 words you could have trimmed from your prompt. Always constrain output first.

### Five Rules Every Developer Must Follow

1. **One task per session** — start a new chat for each distinct problem
2. **Match model to complexity** — don't use Opus for tasks Haiku can handle
3. **Cache your system prompts** — same system prompt across calls = up to 90% savings
4. **Set `max_tokens` on every API call** — never leave it open-ended
5. **Use XML tags** — structured prompts produce structured, predictable outputs

