## 3. Token Optimization Fundamentals

### 3.1 Prompt Caching — Biggest Cost Lever

Cache any content that stays the same across multiple calls. For a team running repeated Magento module reviews or Shopify theme checks, this is the most impactful single change.

**Cache write cost:** 1.25× normal input price (one-time)
**Cache read cost:** 0.1× normal input price (every subsequent call)
**Break-even:** After just 2 calls on the same cached content

```javascript
// Standard caching pattern — works for all three stacks
const response = await anthropic.messages.create({
  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',
  max_tokens: 1024,
  system: [
    {
      type: 'text',
      // ✅ Cache your stable system prompt — project conventions, coding standards
      text: SYSTEM_PROMPT,
      cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' }
    },
    {
      type: 'text',
      // ✅ Cache static context — API docs, schema definitions, style guides
      text: STATIC_CONTEXT,
      cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' }
    }
  ],
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: dynamicUserQuery   // ❌ Never cache — changes every call
    }
  ]
});
```

**What to cache per stack:**

| Stack | Cache This | Don't Cache |
|---|---|---|
| Magento | Module coding standards, EAV schema summary, GraphQL schema | Specific product data, live error messages |
| MERN | Project folder structure, API contract spec, DB schema | User session data, dynamic query params |
| Shopify | Theme architecture docs, store config summary, Polaris guidelines | Cart state, customer data, live metafields |

### 3.2 Output Constraints — Always Specify

```
// ✅ CORRECT: Constrained output
"Return ONLY a JSON object: {file, line, issue, fix}. No explanation. No markdown."

// ❌ WRONG: Open-ended
"Review this code and tell me what's wrong."
```

**Recommended `max_tokens` budgets:**

| Task | max_tokens |
|---|---|
| Classification / categorisation | 50–100 |
| Single function / component | 400–600 |
| Full module / page component | 800–1200 |
| Architecture review | 1500–2000 |
| Full feature with tests | 2000–3000 |

### 3.3 Batch API — 50% Off for Async Work

Use Batch API for any job that does not need an immediate response:

- Nightly code quality scans across all repos
- Weekly security review of Magento custom modules
- Bulk product description generation for Shopify
- Automated test generation runs
- Documentation generation from codebases

```javascript
// Submit a batch job
const batch = await anthropic.messages.batches.create({
  requests: myPrompts.map((prompt, i) => ({
    custom_id: `job-${i}`,
    params: {
      model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',
      max_tokens: 1024,
      messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }]
    }
  }))
});

// Poll for results (up to 24h turnaround)
const results = await anthropic.messages.batches.results(batch.id);
```

### 3.4 Context Window Management

The context window fills with every message, file read, and tool call. Performance degrades as it fills — Claude begins to "forget" earlier instructions.

| Context Level | Action |
|---|---|
| 0–50% | Work normally |
| 50–75% | Scope requests tightly, avoid large file reads |
| 75–90% | Run `/compact` in Claude Code or start summarising |
| 90%+ | **Start a new chat immediately** |

