## 4. Prompt Engineering Standards

### 4.1 The Standard Prompt Template

Use this structure for all API calls across all three stacks. Consistency enables caching and makes debugging easier.

```xml
<system_context>
  You are a senior [Magento/MERN/Shopify] developer at Krish TechnoLabs.
  [Stack-specific expertise description]
  Always respond in the format specified in <output_format>.
  Never add explanations unless explicitly asked.
</system_context>

<task>
  [Single, specific task. One task per prompt — never combine multiple jobs.]
</task>

<context>
  [Relevant background: project name, relevant files, current behaviour]
</context>

<constraints>
  - Max response: [N] tokens
  - Output format: [JSON / YAML / PHP / JSX / Liquid]
  - Scope: [specific files or modules only]
  - Do not: [regenerate unchanged code / explain the obvious / add boilerplate]
</constraints>

<examples>
  [2–5 input → output pairs demonstrating the exact format you want]
</examples>

<data>
  [Runtime data: code snippet, error log, API response — paste here]
</data>
```

### 4.2 XML Tag Reference

| Tag | Cache? | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `<system_context>` | ✅ Yes | Role, expertise, output style |
| `<task>` | ❌ No | Specific job this call |
| `<context>` | ✅ If static | Project background, architecture notes |
| `<constraints>` | ✅ Yes | Token limits, format, scope |
| `<examples>` | ✅ Yes | Input/output demonstrations |
| `<data>` | ❌ No | Dynamic runtime data |
| `<thinking>` | ❌ No | Request extended reasoning (Opus only) |

### 4.3 Multi-Shot Examples — Always Include for Structured Output

Without examples, Claude uses its own format judgment. With 2–5 examples, outputs become consistent and parseable.

```xml
<examples>
  <example>
    <input>Function: calculateTax(price, rate) throws TypeError on null input</input>
    <output>{"file": "utils/tax.js", "line": 12, "issue": "Missing null guard", "fix": "Add: if (!price || !rate) return 0;"}</output>
  </example>
  <example>
    <input>SQL query runs in 8s on products table (2M rows)</input>
    <output>{"file": "Model/ResourceModel/Product.php", "line": 45, "issue": "Missing index on sku column", "fix": "Add: ALTER TABLE catalog_product_entity ADD INDEX idx_sku (sku);"}</output>
  </example>
</examples>
```

