## 8. Claude Code — Cross-Stack Practices

### 8.1 Installation & Daily Workflow

```bash
# Install
npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code

# Start session in project root — CLAUDE.md auto-loads
cd /path/to/project && claude

# Essential session commands
/cost          # Check token usage before expensive operations
/compact       # Compress history when context > 75% full
/clear         # Fresh start for new unrelated task
/model         # Switch model mid-session if complexity changes
/review        # Trigger code review on current files
```

### 8.2 Task Scoping — Most Important Habit

The most common token-wasting mistake is asking Claude to read entire codebases when only one area is relevant.

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT — scoped, specific
"Review the checkout flow in app/code/Krish/Checkout/. 
 Focus only on the payment observer and order placement plugin.
 Return security issues only."

# ❌ WRONG — reads everything, burns context fast
"Review our entire Magento codebase for security issues."
```

### 8.3 Subagents for Parallel Work

For large tasks across multiple files or services, Claude Code can spawn subagents that run in parallel — dramatically reducing wall-clock time.

```
"Use subagents to simultaneously:
 1. Review all React components in /client/src/components for accessibility
 2. Review all Express routes in /server/src/routes for security
 3. Review all Mongoose models for missing indexes
 
 Each subagent returns JSON findings. Merge into a single prioritised report."
```

### 8.4 Piping Real Data

```bash
# Magento — pipe logs directly
tail -n 100 var/log/exception.log | claude \
  "Classify these errors by type and suggest fixes. Return JSON: [{error_type, count, fix}]"

# MERN — pipe test output
npm test 2>&1 | claude \
  "Identify failing tests and their likely cause. Return JSON: [{test_name, file, likely_cause}]"

# Shopify — pipe theme check output
shopify theme check --output json | claude \
  "Summarise critical issues only. Return JSON: [{file, issue, fix}]. Max 10 items."
```

