### 9.3 Do / Don't Matrix

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|---|---|
| One task per chat session | Ask Claude to review entire codebases at once |
| Set `max_tokens` on every API call | Leave token limits open-ended |
| Cache system prompts and static context | Repeat the same context in every message |
| Use Batch API for async/overnight jobs | Run bulk analysis in real-time API |
| Pipe real data using `<data>` tags | Describe the problem vaguely without data |
| Start new chat when context hits 75% | Keep building context until errors appear |
| Store reusable prompts in version control | Recreate prompts from memory each time |
| Use Haiku for classification/simple tasks | Default everything to Sonnet or Opus |
| Provide 2–5 examples for structured output | Expect consistent format without examples |

### 9.4 Monthly Cost Review Process

1. Export API usage from console.anthropic.com
2. Break down by: model tier, cache hit rate, output vs input ratio
3. Identify the top 3 highest-cost prompt patterns
4. Review whether any can move to Batch API or a cheaper model
5. Update shared prompt library with optimised versions

> 🎯 **Target metrics:** Cache hit rate > 60% | Output/Input ratio < 0.3 | Batch share > 30% of total volume

